1 NOTE {geni:about_me} This ancestor appears to be the initial ancestor giving us entry into the dynasty of China......linking us through our ancestors to the Khazars and into the Europeans.
2 CONT __________________________________________
2 CONT Answering the former user's comment:
2 CONT Yes, during the the Tang Dynasty, it took place around 23 times that a Chinese Princess was conceded to a foreign State sovereign or some other important figure in the Royal House, as a Diplomatic gesture, mostly after a War, or t
2 CONC o prevent such eventuality.. Those 23 cases happened only between the Uyghur Khaganate and Tang. But there exist up to 100 such cases of intermarriage with Tibet, the West Turks, the East Turks, etc, in a longer period of time bef
2 CONC ore and afer the Tang Dynasty (0609 —› 0906)
2 CONT See: 
2 CONT [https://www.researchgate.net/publication/389343139_Diplomatic_Marriages_Between_the_Tang_and_Uyghur_Dynasties Diplomatic Marriages Between the Tang and Uyghur Dynasties]
2 CONT
2 CONT As I do not understand Chinese, as well as a great number of geni users, I took help to translate what I originally found here, and what I get I'm pretty sure is at least 95% acceptable. Help those who are able to
2 CONT
2 CONT 【(Luoyang, Henan)】 Yuan Humo
2 CONT Chinese: [Northern Wei] '''Princess Changle''' [(Luoyang, Henan)] '''Yuan Humo'''
2 CONT Gender: Female
2 CONT Birth: estimated between 509 and 509
2 CONT China
2 CONT Death: Turkmenistan
2 CONT Immediate Family:
2 CONT Daughter of Yuan Baoju, Emperor Wen of Western Wei and NN
2 CONT Wife of
2 CONT Istämi, King of the First Turkic Khaganate;
2 CONT Ziebel Tong Yabgu Khan de los Turcos (.);
2 CONT Yuwen Jue Yuwen Jue;
2 CONT Yu Wenzhen (Miotou);
2 CONT Wei Shikang 伟世康; 
2 CONT Yu Chijiong
2 CONT Mother of
2 CONT Qaqim-khaqan (Kayen) of the Turks, Princess of the Turks;
2 CONT T'ung Yabghu Ziebal, Khagan of the Khazars
2 CONT [(Jingzhao Duling)] Webster
2 CONT Sister of
2 CONT Yuan Jian;
2 CONT Yuan Ning;
2 CONT Yuan Gong 元公, Prince Wu of Western Wei;
2 CONT 【(Luoyang, Henan)】 Yuan Confucian;
2 CONT Princess Anle of Western Wei;
2 CONT Princess Yiyang of Western Wei
2 CONT Half sister of
2 CONT Yuan Qin, Emperor Fei (deposed) of Western Wei
2 CONT Yuan Wu, Prince Wudu of Westerm Wei
2 CONT The very first 2 lines give us:
2 CONT Family name: Yuan
2 CONT Personal Name: Humo
2 CONT Patronymic: From ¡ of Louyang, Henan, Northern Wei
2 CONT Or Clan: Henan from Louyang
2 CONT House: Yuan, Northern Wei
