1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://cbdb.fas.harvard.edu/cbdbapi/person.php?id=1038 '''Li Hong''' 李宏] [1038] His ancestors descended from the Tang Xiping Wang, Longxi Li(2) Sheng [3529]. Sheng's grandson, You [4172], moved from Jingzhao, Cha
2 CONC ngan xian to Yuanzhou, Yichun xian. His son, Xianyong [4173], retired to Jizhou, Lushan to compose poetry. Hong(2)'s great great grandfather and Sheng's 6th generation descendant, Li(2) Hanzhang [1025], first moved to Xuanzhou whe
2 CONC n he was appointed prefect and remained there permanently. Hong(2) was called a Xuancheng aristocrat (shidafu). His son-in-law, Weng(1) Shengzhi [4032], had the same generational name as Weng(1) Yanguo's [1956] grandsons and grand
2 CONC nephews. His grandson-in-law, Lu(9) Dezhong [3658], was Lu(9) Guangwen's [1313] son. Anhui TZ, 154.14a; Zhang Kuo, WJ, 8.3a; Han Yuanji, WJ, 20.6a-10b; SHY:ZG, 70.47a. CBD, 2, 831. — [https://www.geni.com/projects/CBDB-Hartwell-co
2 CONC llection/46406 RMH]
