1 NAME Shapur /Kayusiyya Bavand/
2 GIVN Shapur
2 _MARNM Kayusiyya Bavand
1 NAME Shapur of the Bavandids
1 SEX M
1 DEAT
2 DATE 825
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * from Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Shapur''' (Persian: شاپور یکم) was the seventh ruler of the Bavand dynasty, who ruled briefly in 825. He was the son and successor of Shahriyar I. Just when Shapur had ascended the Bavandid throne, the Qarinvand Mazyar, whom Sh
2 CONC apur's father Shahriyar I along with Mazyar's uncle Vinda-Umid had expelled from Tabaristan, returned with an Abbasid army, and invaded the territories of Shapur and Vinda-Umid, where he successfully defeated and killed them both.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Sources=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Madelung, W. (1975). "The Minor Dynasties of Northern Iran". In Frye, R.N. The Cambridge History of Iran, Volume 4: From the Arab Invasion to the Saljuqs. Cambridge: Cambridge University Press. pp. 198–249. ISBN 978-0-521-20093-
2 CONC 6.
