2 CONC inheritance. Some disposed of considerable funds as witnessed by their charitable benefactions. Toghril Beg's chief wife Altun-Jan held estates in Iraq. She died in 452/1060 and bequeathed her estates and pensions to the caliph's 
2 CONC daughter. Toghril assigned these to the latter when the marriage contract between him and the caliph's daughter was finally concluded in 454/1062...
