1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * from [https://books.google.com/books?id=lQjkJOUcVIwC&pg=PA35&lpg=PA35&dq=Zubeida+Khatun,+wife+of+Malik-Shah&source=bl&ots=5h6pZ2rimG&sig=reGhqSBaBsqKwuYCVdSrdzoi_6I&hl=en&sa=X&ei=vWwyVdW8EMnksAT_mIDwBQ&ved=0CDEQ6
2 CONC AEwAw#v=onepage&q=Aka&f=false '''Continuity and Change in Medieval Persia'''] by Ann K.S. Lambton:
2 CONT
2 CONT ...In 462/1069-70 Alp Arslan gave his sister in marriage to the Kurd Hazarasp b. Bankir, who had played a prominent part in Toghril Beg’s relations with the Marvanids and ‘Uqailids. The political nature of this marriage is shown b
2 CONC y the fact that when Hazarasp died in the same year, Alp Arslan gave his widow to the ‘Uqailid Sharaf al-Daula Muslim b. Quraish. 
2 CONT
2 CONT From the [https://books.google.com/books?id=lQjkJOUcVIwC&pg=PA388&lpg=PA388&dq=Sulaiman-Shah,+great+grandson+of+qavurt&source=bl&ots=5h7i0Zo9dG&sig=tyWDVSzDFprN0kjFQPWy_am2eL8&hl=en&sa=X&ei=d_RjVY-NApD_yQSbw4HYCQ&ved=0CC4Q6AEwAg#v
2 CONC =onepage&q=Sulaiman-Shah%2C%20great%20grandson%20of%20qavurt&f=false '''same source'''], she is named Fulana.
