1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * from [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rustam_II '''Wikipedia'''], the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Rustam II''' (Persian: رستم‎), was the twelfth ruler of the Bavand dynasty from 964 to 979. He was the brother and successor of Shahriyar II.
2 CONT
2 CONT Rustam was the son of Sharwin II. In 964, Shahriyar was deposed because of his pro-Ziyarid policies in favor of his pro-Buyid brother Rustam. Rustam was the first Bavand ruler who embraced Shia Islam. Shahriyar later tried to recl
2 CONC aim the Bavand throne by invading Tabaristan with an Samanid army in 968, but with no avail. Rustam died in 979, and was succeeded by his son Al-Marzuban.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Sources=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Madelung, W. (1975). "The Minor Dynasties of Northern Iran". In Frye, R.N. The Cambridge History of Iran, Volume 4: From the Arab Invasion to the Saljuqs. Cambridge: Cambridge University Press. pp. 198–249. ISBN 978-0-521-20093-
2 CONC 6.
2 CONT * Madelung, W. (1984). "ĀL-E BĀVAND (BAVANDIDS)". Encyclopaedia Iranica, Vol. I, Fasc. 7. London u.a.: Routledge & Kegan Paul. pp. 747–753. ISBN 90-04-08114-3.
